# Keeps the build context small and, more importantly, keeps host-only secrets and local
# state out of the image entirely — an .env file sitting in the repo root at build time must
# never end up baked into a layer. Both Dockerfiles build from the repo root (see their own
# comments), so this file lives here, not per-service.

# --- Version control / CI ---
.git/
.github/

# --- Python ---
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
backend/.venv/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov/

# --- Node / Next.js ---
**/node_modules/
frontend/.next/
frontend/next-env.d.ts
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/npm-debug.log*

# --- Env files / secrets ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
frontend/.env.local

# --- Local runtime data (image ships the seed corpus only; runtime state is a volume) ---
backend/data/indices/*.faiss
backend/data/claims.db
backend/data/uploads/
backend/data/synthetic_claims/*.json

# --- Docs / misc (not needed inside either image) ---
docs/
test_scenarios/
*.md
!backend/README.md
infra/

# --- IDE / OS ---
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
